## What “from zero” means

No non-iris V4 subsystem or dose was frozen. The target, historical evidence, product identities, live stocks, all material roles, all design proportions, alternatives and tests were reconsidered. Re-admitting an appropriate old ingredient does not make the old formula the design constraint. This is a ground-up **design candidate**, not a discovery of Dior's secret formula or a demonstrated sensory improvement.

Irotyl is absent by the user's target and smell preference. There is no 30-material ceiling. This candidate has 23 stock lines because eight intended relationships were selected; ingredient count is neither the objective nor proof of complexity. Its dose proportions are locally designed starting hypotheses, not literature-derived optima.

The iris basket is 2,320 µL of prepared stocks, versus 1,050 µL in V4. Orris Liquid is 1,500 µL versus 510 µL; Alpha Ionone is 60 µL versus 120 µL. All other groups were rebalanced. Raw stock volumes do not measure relative perceived contribution.

## TARGET / IDEAL — evidence and design boundary

The desired perfume remains root-led iris with cosmetic powder, restrained fruity ambrette-like movement, fine aromatic entry, warm depth and a cedar/vetiver return. The ideal input would be an authenticated 2011 reference sample and lot-qualified orris/ambrette/wood materials tested blind; none is fabricated from public note descriptions.

Current Dior copy describes iris, ambrette-associated fruity talc and a woody amber setting. Its current Swiss-page disclosure #21961 is not an archived 05443/A concentrate. The 2011 launch report separately describes DHI's lavender/iris/ambrette/pear/powder/cedar/vetiver sequence; cocoa and leather occur in its adjacent EDT discussion. Neither note list is an analytical ingredient list. [Current Dior](https://www.dior.com/en_ch/beauty/products/dior-homme-intense-Y0479201.html) · [2011 report, secondary](https://www.fragrantica.com/news/Dior-Homme-2011-by-Francois-Demachy-Dior-Homme-Intense-2011-Francois-Demachy-Dior-J-adore-Eau-de-Toilette-2011-2383.html)

The 2025 irone study compares an orris absolute, commercial IRONE ALPHA, synthesized beta-irone and beta-ionone. Its small descriptive panel and impurity findings argue against treating these as interchangeable. It supplies neither a dose optimum nor an assay of the user's bottles. Beta-irone is not Beta Ionone and is not added here. [Yamazaki and Miyazaki, 2025](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-08925-z)

## Eight connected facets — hypotheses, not observed layers

| Intended facet | Materials, not historical ingredient claims | Relationship to establish | Evaluation window / failure |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Aromatic contour | Lavender, Linalyl Acetate, Coriander | A fine aromatic/spicy entry hands into floral iris rather than a separate lavender perfume. | 0–5 min; aromatic dominance or culinary spice fails. |
| 2. Fruit-to-ambrette relation | Verdox, Benzyl Acetate, Ambrettolide | A restrained green-fruit glint becomes musky/talc-like beside iris. | Opening into heart; literal apple/banana/candy dominance fails. |
| 3. Root-rich centre | Orris Liquid, Alpha Irone | The preferred supplied Orris product leads; the irone stock is an independently testable accent. | Heart and later return; root identity must survive powder and wood. |
| 4. Cosmetic powder with violet movement | Alpha Isomethyl Ionone, Alpha Ionone | Powder has body without becoming a detached violet flower; it frames the root. | Heart; compare root exposure and powder integration separately. |
| 5. Air around the dense centre | Hedione, provisional Benzyl Salicylate | Separation and a soft cosmetic surface, not another floral accord. | Heart; first-line omissions test redundant film/air helpers. |
| 6. Warm interior and darker grain | Tonkarome, Isobutavan, Cashmeran, Kephalis | Coumarinic/vanillic warmth and a darker woody-textile seam sit beneath iris. | Heart to late heart; pastry, named tobacco or amberwood takeover fails. |
| 7. Dry wood and root return | Virginia cedar, Indian vetiver, Vetival, Iso E Super, small Ebanol seam | Literal cedar grain and dry root emerge through a smoother wood/skin transition. | Late heart/drydown; anonymous wood, pencil shavings or sandalwood takeover fails. |
| 8. Powder-to-skin persistence | Ambrettolide, Ethylene Brassylate | Fruity skin relation and powdered body are separate hypotheses, not a three-musk default. | Late heart/drydown; a musk blanket that erases iris fails. |

Benzyl Benzoate is structural and receives no layer credit. Other low-odor helpers receive no independent note credit without evidence. The phases overlap; the headings do not promise a clockwork sequence on skin.

## CURRENT-INVENTORY BUILD

**Nominal bottle:** 30 mL. **Raw-stock concentrate:** 6,000 µL. **Ethanol 96% addition:** 24,000 µL. **Nominal sum:** 30,000 µL. The 20% label is raw-stock concentrate v/v under additive-volume convention, not 20% neat odorants, not 20% w/w. Contraction, transfer loss, homogeneity and stability are unmeasured.

For each delivered stock mass m_i and known supplied-product mass fraction f_i, product mass = f_i × m_i and product ppm w/w in concentrate = 1,000,000 × f_i × m_i / Σm_i. Where the supplied product is a mixture, this is product mass, not pure irone, coumarin or another constituent. Pure-component ppm additionally needs a lot-supported assay.

Measure delivered mass for every row and total concentrate mass before claiming exact ppm. A w/w stock cannot yield exact active µL by multiplying raw volume by its mass fraction. No prepared-stock density is invented. The model may use such proxies or registry densities; those outputs are explicitly non-authoritative screening estimates.

