All main-card transfers are at least 20 µL; the exactly half-size 15 mL card has no transfer below 10 µL. Do not scale further without a separately specified, labeled working-stock design.

## Physical-stock identity and authority limits

The live inventory was read completely. Its SHA-256 at design time was 5da7ecdab4ce9c297f95a61051b38d9183f796c1971dd276546ef15c7856c497. Later direct-user stock receipts were independently read in the canonical checkout:

- September 5 Orris receipt: **9% w/w in DEP**, stock ID `inventory:user-20260905:d83ef5ae6b6ecfc22f72`. This supersedes older 30% and carrier-unknown entries for design selection.
- September 4 AIMI receipt: “Givaudan AIMI” and “Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure)” were confirmed to describe **one physical bottle**, not two interchangeable grades. This corrects V4's unresolved-two-label caution; it does not generalize to other methyl-ionone grades.
- September 4 Indian vetiver receipt identifies the owned Indian volume-grade EO.
- September 4 Ambrettolide receipt: **10% w/w in DPG**, user-confirmed homogeneous and pipettable.
- September 4 Tonkarome receipt: **20% w/w in TEC**, a supplied base prepared from 4 g product + 16 g TEC.
- Alpha Irone remains **10% w/w in DEP**. Cashmeran is **neat**, despite stale display text suggesting a desired 20% preparation. Ethylene Brassylate is **neat/as supplied**.

Receipt paths and hashes are recorded in the design JSON and research record. At the original design checkpoint these receipts had not been imported into c4d5, causing the historical stock-binding failures. The explicit September 5 reconciliation now connects only the five selected records through a validated successor; it does not replace this worktree's other stock records or holds. The canonical Orris stock ID above remains source provenance, not the new local runtime stock ID. The pour card still requires matching physical labels, adequate remaining volume and homogeneous stocks. No remaining quantity is invented.

The Orris YAML/composite model still contains an old stock description and an 82.5% modeled irone pool derived from a catalog range. **That is not the user's lot assay.** It must not be promoted to exact product composition or sensory dominance. Missing densities, commercial-mixture pseudo-MW/ODT and supplier/runtime VP differences further limit modeled OAV.

## Every selected material re-admitted independently

| Material | Fresh role decision | Omission or alternative test |
|---|---|---|
| Hedione | Floral air around iris; not a new jasmine subject. | Zero arm tests an opaque heart; compare a lighter floral support only if that deficit is repeatable. |
| Iso E Super | Diffuse transition from iris into literal cedar grain. | Omit while keeping cedar fixed; generic wood volume is not a successful transition. |
| Vetival | Smoother dry woody transition ahead of natural vetiver. | Compare natural vetiver alone, Vetival alone in this role, and both; retain both only for a distinct useful difference. |
| Benzyl Benzoate | Structural/vehicle provision, not an olfactory layer. | No fixation or clarity benefit claimed without a test; omit in a vehicle-controlled trial, not as a universal replacement liquid. |
| Benzyl Salicylate | Provisional cosmetic-film support beside powder. | First-line omission candidate; reject without repeatable texture benefit. Below-threshold model output earns no perceptible-note credit. |
| Vetiver EO (India) | Owned Indian vetiver: dry root counterline under cedar. | Compare cedar alone; excessive smoke or soil is failure. Not authenticated Haitian or Dior vetiver. |
| Cedarwood oil Virginia | Recognizable dry cedar grain and late iris-to-wood return. | Compare omission; pencil-shaving dominance that erases iris is failure. |
| Cashmeran | Powder-to-warm-wood textile seam. | Compare zero and Kephalis-only; distinct texture must survive beyond an increase in woody strength. |
| Ebanol | Small creamy edge at the cedar-to-skin boundary. | Not a sandalwood accord or historical ingredient claim; compare zero and Sandalore as alternatives, never automatic stacking. |
| Kephalis | Darker woody-amber interior joining violet, lavender and late woods. | Compare zero, Cashmeran-only and both. Named tobacco or amberwood becoming the subject rejects this branch. |
| Ambrettolide | Fruity skin-musk relation connecting fruit, iris and talc. | Proxy for part of the ambrette image, not whole ambrette extract. Compare single-musk and pair omissions with carrier matched. |
| Ethylene Brassylate | Powdered body behind iris, distinct hypothesis from fruity Ambrettolide. | Compare Ambrettolide alone and Exaltolide/Romandolide alternatives when stock-qualified; a smooth but anonymous musk blanket fails. |
| Lavender EO High Altitude | Aromatic entry that hands over to iris. | Use the exact owned high-altitude French stock; compare zero or the separately owned BONTAUX grade, not silent substitution. |
| Linalyl Acetate | Adjustable lavender-to-fruit/floral ester transition. | Compare lavender alone. Extra duration of lavender without a better handoff is redundancy. |
| Orris Liquid | User-selected supplied-product root lead; powder, root and creamy irregularity remain a whole-product hypothesis. | Compare reference-qualified orris products only as alternatives. No pure-irone amount or Dior-product match inferred from supplier marketing. |
| Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure) | Cosmetic powder body surrounding the preferred Orris product. | Known aliases identify one confirmed bottle; they do not license other gamma/coeur grades. Test whether less powder reveals more root. |
| Alpha Irone | Independent iris/root accent, not a substitute for the whole Orris product. | Compare zero at fixed Orris; known preparation does not certify pure alpha-irone or an isomer profile. |
| Alpha Ionone | Restrained violet movement between fruit and powder. | Omit at fixed Orris/methyl ionone; separate violet-flower identity or no useful loss rejects the helper. |
| Tonkarome | Coumarinic fabric warmth under the iris, not a tonka lead. | Supplied base, not pure coumarin. Compare zero and a basis-qualified Coumarin stock as an alternative. |
| Isobutavan | Vanillic seam distinct from the coumarinic fabric. | Compare zero and a stock-qualified vanillin alternative; recognizable pastry or buttercream is failure. |
| Coriander Essential Oil | Fine spicy/aromatic contour at the lavender-to-iris entry. | Creative addition, not a claimed Dior ingredient. Compare zero; recognizable culinary spice or no repeatable contour rejects it. |
| Verdox | Green fruit-to-wood glint carried toward Ambrettolide. | Pear is an accord outcome to test, not the ingredient identity. Apple/candy recognition that competes with iris is failure. |
| Benzyl Acetate | Small floral-fruit bridge distinct from Verdox green wood. | Provisional omission priority: lavender ester/Hedione may already bridge the gap. Banana/jasmine intrusion rejects it. |

## Old helpers removed and serious alternatives

| Material / group | From-zero disposition |
|---|---|
| Romandolide | Removed. Maker description supports powdery/balsamic volume, not the inherited unique outward-projection claim. It remains an alternative to EB, not an automatic third musk. |
| Mimosa Absolute | Removed from main build. Yellow-flower/powder alternative only; not necessary to the target and preparation basis remains unresolved. |
| Osmanthus Absolute | Removed from main build. A separate fruit/violet/suede bridge experiment can compete with the explicit fruit bridge; apricot intrusion is a risk. |
| Linalool | Removed as a separate ingredient. Lavender and the chosen aromatic/floral supports already supply overlapping functions. |
| Sandalore | Removed. Ebanol is a small independently selected wood-to-skin seam, not a one-for-one equivalent or mandatory sandalwood accord. |
| Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | Removed. Fruit flash is not mandatory, and the current prepared-stock basis is insufficient for exact active mass. |
| Irotyl | Excluded by user instruction; never restored for a generic iris-family gate. No proprietary Dior absence proof is claimed from public notes. |
| Orivone | Serious optional earthy-root contrast, but the maker's camphoraceous edge risks displacing the chosen rich root. Not silently described as buttery or necessarily in Dior. |
| Carrot Seed / Dihydro Beta Ionone / Ultralia / other iris grades | Considered alternatives, not extra layers by default. Require exact product identity and a useful controlled difference. |
| Exaltolide | Different skin-texture alternative to EB; prepared-stock basis unresolved for exact mass. Not stacked without a distinct role test. |
| Heliotropal / Piperonal | Powder/almond alternative, but the confirmed stock is neat solid, not a verified 10% liquid preparation. No direct µL solid dose invented. |
| Cocoa / Suederal | Optional creative dark/suede branches only, not established DHI2011 ingredients. Current stock-binding gaps and target drift exclude them from this first card. |
| Elemi / citrus / moss / incense / oud / rose / heavy resins | No demonstrated target-linked gap warrants another recognizer. This is a scope choice, not a claim that all such pairs chemically clash. |

The full inventory-category and hidden-fixative review did not make low VP, prestige, ownership, or availability sufficient reason to add a material. Musk pairwise tests are Ambrettolide alone, EB alone in the assigned role, both, and role-matched alternatives. Cashmeran × Kephalis, natural vetiver × Vetival, and Tonkarome × Isobutavan also need interaction/omission tests.

