This is the same explicitly approximate ethanol/water convention used by V4 at 305 K. These are modeled constituents of the already prescribed 24,000 µL Ethanol 96%, not extra transfers or measurements. Prepared-stock DEP/DPG/TEC remain unresolved in the physical mole/mass model; declaring this solvent proxy does not establish full-matrix accuracy, exact ppm or skin behavior.

## Testing and knowledge contract

See the research record for carrier-matched omissions, proportion experiments, blind hedonic assessment and decision rules. No sensory observations exist yet; nothing in a gate pass teaches the actual smell of this blend. Model-specific warnings can produce documented data-quality findings and proposed experiments, not learned preference or a changed model weight.

**Pipeline screening:** pending at initial creation. This section will be completed using the current report and full formatter output. All final safety, physical and sensory authority remains HOLD/NOT TESTED until supported separately.

## Pipeline Analysis

**Secondary reference selected — 2026-09-06:** DHP 2025, as requested by the user. Qualitative iris/amber comparison only; the local model's unverified ingredient requirements and numerical ratios are not accepted. DHI 2011 remains the target and the archetype of the diagnostic below. No dose changed and Irotyl remains excluded. See the DHP reference section of the scientific audit for the source and scope; no DHP-specific test pass is claimed.

**Scientific-data audit (current): 106 PASS / 36 WARN / 3 FAIL / 1 SKIP; release HOLD.** Orris Liquid and Tonkarome OAVs are UNKNOWN. All 23 doses are unchanged and all 23 delivered masses remain unmeasured. Earlier numeric reports and design-time scientific-data descriptions are historical; the old Orris composite has now been withdrawn. See the full scientific-data audit at the end of this section, the September 5 Orris/Tonkarome research audit and the V5 mass/safety worksheet. This report notice belongs to the analysis, not the hashed formula definition.

